WEBVTT

00:09.175 --> 00:10.844
Hey, slow down.

00:10.927 --> 00:12.762
Y'all gonna hurt yourselves.

00:14.597 --> 00:16.558
Here, you forgot your keys again--

00:20.729 --> 00:23.023
-Can I help you?
-Mrs. Davis, I'm Detective Harper.

00:23.106 --> 00:26.234
-This is my partner, Detective Viggiano.
-Look, Deon ain't here.

00:26.317 --> 00:29.029
All right, he ain't come home last night,
and I don't know where he at.

00:29.112 --> 00:32.449
So please don't bother asking.
All right, we-- We good now?

00:32.532 --> 00:33.908
Oh, we're great, yeah.

00:33.992 --> 00:36.453
Deon, not so much.

00:37.037 --> 00:40.540
Deon's dead.
We're here to search your premises.

00:40.623 --> 00:42.292
Here's your warrant.

00:42.876 --> 00:46.838
W-wait, hold up. Get the fuck
out of my house, you motherfucking pig!

00:47.589 --> 00:50.842
-What the fuck?
-I want you to search the bedrooms first.

00:50.925 --> 00:54.387
Hold up. Y'all tell me my husband dead,
come in here, shit, and fuck it up?

00:54.471 --> 00:55.847
Y'all got me fucked up.

00:55.930 --> 00:57.974
Fuck all y'all motherfuckers!

00:58.058 --> 01:01.394
Yeah, fuck you,
fuck you, and fuck you too!

01:27.003 --> 01:28.296
What do you want?

01:30.256 --> 01:33.551
-Just wanna holler at you.
-You can holler at my lawyers, man.

01:33.635 --> 01:36.888
-Ain't like that, player.
-You really wanna do this?

01:36.971 --> 01:38.848
Here? Right now?

01:38.932 --> 01:42.769
This ain't a business call.
It's personal, man-to-man type shit.

01:42.852 --> 01:45.105
Just want a few minutes, that's it.

01:49.818 --> 01:52.445
-You on the clock.
-All right, say no more.

01:53.113 --> 01:54.989
I knew you'd be here today.

01:55.073 --> 01:58.201
My mama, my big bro,
they buried right up around that bend.

01:58.785 --> 02:01.871
-My condolences.
-Man, they been dead a long time.

02:02.539 --> 02:04.874
I gotta focus
on what's in front of me now.

02:05.792 --> 02:09.003
-Yeah, me too.
-I was thinking on my drive up here, man.

02:09.087 --> 02:10.130
You were right.

02:10.839 --> 02:13.550
Back at the gala when we first
chopped it up and all that, I mean.

02:13.633 --> 02:16.261
View Park, Baldwin Hills,
practically cousins.

02:16.761 --> 02:19.097
We are neighbors.

02:19.180 --> 02:21.057
My dumb ass. I've been running around

02:21.141 --> 02:23.977
trying to retrace your crimes
for years to find you,

02:24.060 --> 02:27.814
and you were right across Stocker
the whole motherfucking time?

02:27.897 --> 02:30.108
Our wives kicking it together,
and all that.

02:30.191 --> 02:34.028
Shit, man, another life,
me and you, we could've been homies.

02:34.112 --> 02:35.738
But then that had me thinking.

02:35.822 --> 02:39.450
No matter how much we have in common,

02:40.285 --> 02:43.329
our similarities end in one simple way.

02:43.413 --> 02:45.874
You kill innocent people.

02:46.833 --> 02:49.127
Like my trainee, Detective Manny Shaw.

02:49.210 --> 02:51.462
That's the difference
between men like you and me.

02:51.546 --> 02:53.756
Men like me are the reason
why men like you make a living.

02:53.840 --> 02:56.968
-You a criminal.
-No, I'm a job creator, see.

02:57.594 --> 03:00.013
You spend all this time
trying to prove I'm something other

03:00.096 --> 03:02.015
than what people believe me to be.

03:02.098 --> 03:04.851
But allow me to let you in
on a little secret, Stiles.

03:04.934 --> 03:06.686
You're not fooling anyone.

03:06.769 --> 03:09.731
Hiding behind your badge
and your loud street clothes out there

03:09.814 --> 03:11.357
trying to impress the oppressed.

03:12.275 --> 03:15.945
Your bravado and arrests, they can't hide
the fact that I know who you really are.

03:17.155 --> 03:18.448
A nigga with a gun.

03:19.073 --> 03:22.368
A fucking thug in designer apparel.

03:22.452 --> 03:23.870
-Look at you.
-Like you?

03:23.953 --> 03:25.246
Sure.

03:25.330 --> 03:28.875
Like me, just not smart enough
to do better economically.

03:28.958 --> 03:30.043
Oh, that's funny, nigga.

03:30.126 --> 03:32.545
I got over half a dozen medals
and commendations for my career…

03:32.629 --> 03:35.298
Stop! Stop! Stop talking like that.

03:35.381 --> 03:39.761
You may act like a cop, quack like a cop,
you may do cop shit, but you're not.

03:39.844 --> 03:41.679
You're fucking cutthroat, just like me.

03:41.763 --> 03:44.766
And there's nothing you can do
to prove otherwise. You know how I know?

03:45.350 --> 03:48.019
Killers recognize killers, Stiles.

03:48.102 --> 03:49.729
You're one of us.

03:51.189 --> 03:53.775
As a matter of fact, we're so alike,

03:53.858 --> 03:56.361
you've been obsessed with me
since the moment we met.

03:56.444 --> 03:58.404
-Remember that day?
-I think about it all the time.

03:58.488 --> 04:01.282
Just like I said, obsessed. Look at you.

04:01.366 --> 04:05.370
And now you're mad because I won.
I'm fucking done. I'm out the game.

04:05.453 --> 04:08.248
I'm about to spend the rest of my life
on top of the world

04:08.331 --> 04:12.293
while you watch all the way
from the fucking cheap seats!

04:12.377 --> 04:13.836
God bless, nigga.

04:16.130 --> 04:17.632
I have a confession.

04:18.591 --> 04:19.968
I lied.

04:21.261 --> 04:22.595
There you go.

04:24.097 --> 04:26.057
We do have some business to discuss.

04:27.600 --> 04:30.937
See, I got some good news,
and I got some bad news.

04:31.020 --> 04:35.775
Good news, there's a light
at the end of the tunnel, brother.

04:35.858 --> 04:39.279
Bad news, it's a train coming at you.

04:40.613 --> 04:42.240
LAPD!

04:42.323 --> 04:44.951
We're executing a warrant
for Coltrane Wilder and Wilder Holdings.

04:54.168 --> 04:56.754
We got a warrant.
Please step away from your station.

04:56.838 --> 04:59.507
Do not touch any property
or take it with you.

04:59.590 --> 05:03.553
The business
that we have to discuss, Mr. Wilder,

05:04.554 --> 05:06.514
is that you have no business

05:07.140 --> 05:08.474
and no money.

05:08.558 --> 05:12.061
Everything is frozen.

05:12.145 --> 05:15.398
Your pristine
Jet Magazine cover lifestyle? Yeah.

05:15.481 --> 05:17.108
Black history.

05:17.692 --> 05:20.111
Your hood TED Talks
you be giving to kids in the community?

05:20.194 --> 05:21.696
Black history.

05:22.739 --> 05:25.074
Your little secret crime clubhouse?

05:25.158 --> 05:27.201
Black fucking history.

05:27.285 --> 05:29.037
And it's all thanks to…

05:30.038 --> 05:31.039
Deon.

05:32.081 --> 05:33.541
God bless him.

05:34.083 --> 05:36.627
Hey, hey. Hey, man, don't worry.

05:36.711 --> 05:39.714
He ain't snitched. He burnt it all up.

05:40.715 --> 05:42.300
I tried to bring him in.

05:43.551 --> 05:45.887
Oh shit. You ain't hear?

05:45.970 --> 05:47.347
You ain't know?

05:49.390 --> 05:51.517
Deon, he ain't with us no more.

05:52.977 --> 05:54.645
He with the dead homies now.

05:57.607 --> 05:58.608
And next,

05:59.400 --> 06:00.818
you'll be in cuffs.

06:00.902 --> 06:02.987
Maxing out a life sentence

06:03.071 --> 06:07.116
in 23 and 1-hour lockdown
in a 180-yard prison.

06:07.200 --> 06:09.202
Just like I told you.

06:09.285 --> 06:11.245
Because I'm a man of my word.

06:13.373 --> 06:14.874
No need to ask who's winning.

06:16.334 --> 06:18.169
Check the scoreboard, nigga.

06:33.476 --> 06:35.770
-This business is closed, sir.
-Fuck it is.

06:36.646 --> 06:37.980
You can't be in here.

06:38.940 --> 06:42.276
Hey, stop asking her questions.
She doesn't need to speak to you.

06:42.360 --> 06:44.654
-Who are you?
-Coltrane fucking Wilder.

06:44.737 --> 06:46.572
Stop interrogating my receptionist.

06:46.656 --> 06:50.034
-Tell me who the fuck is in charge. Now.
-Keep turning this upside down.

06:50.118 --> 06:53.704
Take every document regarding every
transaction this company's ever made.

06:53.788 --> 06:56.874
You heard the detective. Keep digging.

07:02.755 --> 07:03.840
Okay.

07:03.923 --> 07:04.882
Mm-hmm.

07:05.425 --> 07:08.886
What we got? What we got? Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

07:08.970 --> 07:11.097
Great, look at this shit. Fuck this.

07:11.180 --> 07:12.306
Mazel tov. Hey!

07:13.391 --> 07:15.101
Find me my fucking evidence!

07:15.768 --> 07:18.187
Our evidence.
I brought you in on this, Stiles.

07:18.271 --> 07:19.313
This is my case now.

07:21.524 --> 07:24.694
-You're a real piece of work.
-You don't have to do this this way.

07:24.777 --> 07:29.240
-Ebony, you don't have to watch. Come on.
-This is unnecessary. We know each other.

07:29.323 --> 07:33.744
You don't know me. You know my wife.
I know that your husband is a criminal.

07:33.828 --> 07:35.746
That's the extent
of our relationship, sis.

07:35.830 --> 07:38.666
You think Coltrane's doing
something illegal? He's not.

07:38.749 --> 07:40.251
There's nothing here.

07:40.835 --> 07:44.547
He's not the person that you think he is,
and we haven't done anything wrong.

07:44.630 --> 07:47.758
Ebony, you're giving me a headache.
Look, you're playing in my face now.

07:47.842 --> 07:50.803
'Cause either you deserve the Oscar
or you straight dickmatized.

07:54.223 --> 07:55.433
Excuse me.

07:59.228 --> 08:03.441
Why are we going in this room?
What are you doing? This is insane!

08:03.524 --> 08:07.069
-What? Can you stop that, please? Stop.
-There's a warrant in your hand for that.

08:07.153 --> 08:08.112
Enough, Isaiah!

08:08.196 --> 08:09.739
If you continue to interfere,

08:09.822 --> 08:12.617
I will have to detain you
outside on the curb in cuffs.

08:13.409 --> 08:16.454
-He's got shit hidden somewhere.
-Check the walls, Lieutenant?

08:18.289 --> 08:19.123
Yeah.

08:20.249 --> 08:21.667
This is excessive, Stiles.

08:21.751 --> 08:25.087
Excessive is Coltrane Wilder and his co-Ds
running around Los Angeles

08:25.171 --> 08:29.550
robbing, killing people,
police officers with impunity for years.

08:30.134 --> 08:32.136
You're off the deep end.

08:34.388 --> 08:35.598
Swim away.

08:40.269 --> 08:41.437
Hit that shit.

09:10.424 --> 09:14.053
We need to leave the country immediately
and never set foot on US soil again!

09:14.136 --> 09:16.764
Ebony, listen to me!
Lemme tell you what happens when we leave.

09:16.847 --> 09:19.934
We get an indictment
and a conviction in absentia.

09:20.017 --> 09:23.104
Then we're stuck overseas
as fugitives for the rest of our lives.

09:23.187 --> 09:24.480
Is that what you want, baby?

09:25.565 --> 09:27.567
Have you thought about
what life that is for a child?

09:27.650 --> 09:30.069
Looking over our shoulders at every turn.

09:30.152 --> 09:32.238
No, I can't have that on my conscience.

09:32.321 --> 09:38.160
Right now… Right now
the wisest choice is to stay the course.

09:38.786 --> 09:40.830
The only way out is through, baby.

09:44.041 --> 09:45.710
You saw what he did to Zahir's room?

09:46.794 --> 09:50.631
That's what Stiles
is trying to do to our life. Destroy it.

09:51.841 --> 09:53.175
Destroy us.

09:54.594 --> 09:56.304
I love you, Coltrane.

09:57.597 --> 10:02.226
And I've always trusted your leadership
to do what's best for our family.

10:02.310 --> 10:03.769
But right now,

10:04.895 --> 10:07.189
I need to figure this out on my own

10:07.273 --> 10:09.442
before you end up like Deon.

10:20.911 --> 10:24.165
Okay, so he's here,
but they said they under strict orders.

10:24.248 --> 10:26.834
-So we can't see him.
-It's okay, Big Mama.

10:26.917 --> 10:29.503
We're gonna be straight.
I got this. I promise.

10:30.504 --> 10:34.050
Yeah. All right, I'm on it.
Hey, I'm gonna call you right back.

10:34.133 --> 10:37.303
Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Hey, relax, relax, big man.

10:37.386 --> 10:40.139
-I ain't here for that.
-What the fuck you here for, nigga?

10:41.682 --> 10:44.644
Ladies, I am so sorry for your loss.

10:44.727 --> 10:48.022
I mean, none of us,
we did not want it to go down this way.

10:48.564 --> 10:51.776
Y'all are hurting. Y'all are in pain.
So I'm here to offer my help.

10:51.859 --> 10:55.613
We don't need your motherfucking help.
You lucky my mama and granny here.

10:55.696 --> 10:58.199
I'm gonna have the coroner
let y'all back to see Deon

10:58.282 --> 11:02.161
if Darren will talk to me for two minutes.

11:02.244 --> 11:05.956
It's just 120 seconds of dialogue,
and then y'all can say y'all goodbyes.

11:06.040 --> 11:09.085
-Nigga, is you crazy?
-Darren, baby, please.

11:12.797 --> 11:13.964
Hey, Eddie.

11:14.590 --> 11:17.218
Let's, uh, get that paperwork started
on Gideon Davis.

11:17.301 --> 11:19.553
I'm gonna let them back to see him.
Alright, I'll sign off.

11:19.637 --> 11:21.222
Would you like to follow me?

11:27.353 --> 11:28.646
Mm-mm.

11:29.689 --> 11:30.523
Mm.

11:31.732 --> 11:35.820
Ooh, boy, your circle getting small, Stro.

11:37.113 --> 11:38.406
Finna be a dot soon, nigga.

11:39.573 --> 11:41.283
Yeah, I know that look.

11:41.367 --> 11:42.410
Yeah, you so mad

11:42.493 --> 11:46.163
you would just choke me to death
right here, right now, huh?

11:46.247 --> 11:48.207
Spend the rest of your life
in a jail cell,

11:48.290 --> 11:51.794
smiling once a day
at the fact that you murdered me, right?

11:51.877 --> 11:53.462
-Then what?
-We'd be even, nigga.

11:53.546 --> 11:54.380
That's your plan?

11:54.463 --> 11:57.341
Spend the rest of your life
in a jail cell or worse off, dead?

11:57.425 --> 12:00.678
Tsk. Come on, man, I told you this is
what would happen last time we linked.

12:00.761 --> 12:03.222
-Don't wanna go out like your uncle.
-Watch your fucking mouth.

12:03.305 --> 12:06.225
I didn't mean it like that.
I did, but just chill out, man.

12:06.934 --> 12:10.479
Look, man, you got daughters.
A man's job is to provide for his family.

12:10.563 --> 12:15.901
And in order to do that,
you have to be out here in the real world,

12:15.985 --> 12:19.655
not in a penitentiary,
not in a city morgue right here,

12:19.739 --> 12:21.699
because I know something you don't.

12:21.782 --> 12:25.077
Deon's blood was a direct match
for the DNA we pulled off that detonator

12:25.161 --> 12:27.663
used to blow the walls
out of the jewelry store heist.

12:27.747 --> 12:29.874
I don't know
what you're talking about, bro.

12:30.541 --> 12:32.752
Stro, come on, nigga, for real?

12:33.335 --> 12:37.298
Dog, we know Deon was one
of the four perps who pulled off that job

12:37.381 --> 12:38.883
and killed those two men.

12:38.966 --> 12:41.802
It's only a matter of time
before I pin you and Chris Choi

12:41.886 --> 12:46.390
as members number two and three,
but buss it, I'm a benevolent nigga.

12:47.266 --> 12:50.644
I'm willing to ignore members
number one, two, and three

12:50.728 --> 12:53.314
for member number four, your boy Coltrane.

12:55.065 --> 12:56.066
Mm?

12:56.650 --> 12:58.986
You give me Coltrane,
I'll get you a proffer deal.

12:59.069 --> 13:00.112
Low time.

13:01.822 --> 13:02.948
It's no cap.

13:05.868 --> 13:08.704
I can still give you and your family
a way out of this.

13:11.916 --> 13:15.085
But my offer, just like these streets,
playboy, it's got an expiration date.

13:15.169 --> 13:17.087
So don't fuck around.

13:17.630 --> 13:18.881
Give me Coltrane.

13:33.979 --> 13:35.397
We need to go now.

13:35.481 --> 13:38.526
Let's calm down
and think this out rationally.

13:38.609 --> 13:40.861
Your nervous energy
is not a net positive right now.

13:40.945 --> 13:43.239
Now, you know the protocol
for this type of shit.

13:43.322 --> 13:44.448
You need to be thinking about

13:44.532 --> 13:47.952
what an innocent man's wife
would be doing, and go do that.

13:48.035 --> 13:50.996
You're allowing your hormones and emotions
to override your better judgment.

13:51.080 --> 13:55.125
This is me exercising my better judgment.

13:55.209 --> 13:56.961
For all of us.

13:57.586 --> 13:58.796
Where you going?

13:58.879 --> 14:02.383
I'm done listening to people
tell me when to worry and what to do.

14:02.967 --> 14:05.344
And by the way,
I already contacted our lawyers.

14:05.427 --> 14:08.681
If this doesn't get resolved soon,
we're leaving.

14:08.764 --> 14:11.976
Don't let your street smarts
get blocked by your book smarts, Ivy.

14:13.519 --> 14:17.982
You always call me Ivy League
like it's an insult, but it's not.

14:19.358 --> 14:25.698
I am a strong, smart, educated bitch,
and the bottom line remains.

14:25.781 --> 14:27.658
If you can't show me the way,

14:27.741 --> 14:30.578
then you need to
get the fuck out of my way.

15:02.109 --> 15:03.402
Oh!

15:04.320 --> 15:08.490
Oh my word. He did all of this?

15:08.574 --> 15:10.117
Yes.

15:10.200 --> 15:12.286
That's why I asked you to come.

15:13.120 --> 15:17.082
Isaiah and his goons destroyed everything.

15:18.375 --> 15:20.127
Just to make a point.

15:21.670 --> 15:25.174
Your husband is the case
that Isaiah's been working on?

15:27.259 --> 15:31.138
Oh, Ebony, I'm gonna have
to ask you this straight.

15:31.639 --> 15:32.806
Is Coltrane a criminal?

15:32.890 --> 15:36.393
No, Coltrane is not a criminal.

15:37.311 --> 15:39.355
Did you know Isaiah was gonna do all this?

15:39.438 --> 15:41.148
-No.
-Exactly.

15:41.231 --> 15:46.153
All I know is that whatever your husband
is accusing Coltrane of, he didn't do.

15:51.325 --> 15:56.914
Do you have any idea how much stress
this is causing me and my unborn child?

15:57.831 --> 15:59.416
I can only imagine, uh…

15:59.500 --> 16:03.504
Well, then can you imagine that what
I'm saying to you is true? Because it is.

16:05.506 --> 16:07.675
I don't know what to believe anymore. I…

16:10.052 --> 16:11.720
I know you're my friend.

16:12.930 --> 16:15.599
And I know Isaiah,
he's been acting out at home.

16:17.810 --> 16:19.353
You know what I also know?

16:20.104 --> 16:24.316
That I don't want him
to destroy our relationship also.

16:26.110 --> 16:27.069
Okay?

16:27.778 --> 16:29.655
Sweetie, I'm so sorry.

16:30.698 --> 16:32.116
Thank you, Candace.

16:35.369 --> 16:36.370
I'm sorry.

16:38.038 --> 16:40.457
-Is that Malik?
-Yeah.

16:40.541 --> 16:44.795
-Are you still seeing him tomorrow?
-He wants to meet, maybe do coffee.

16:44.878 --> 16:46.964
I just don't know where to suggest.

16:48.716 --> 16:50.009
I know a place.

16:50.968 --> 16:52.720
You've reached Dr. Candace Stiles.

16:52.803 --> 16:54.263
Please leave a message.

16:54.346 --> 16:56.890
Candace, baby, I'm coming home, uh…

16:56.974 --> 16:59.393
I'm stopping by Amos's for a minute.

16:59.476 --> 17:02.312
You were right.
It's time to bury the hatchet.

17:20.289 --> 17:21.498
What you doing here?

17:22.750 --> 17:26.045
It ain't shit, just, um, heading home,

17:26.128 --> 17:28.630
trying to catch Noah
before he go to sleep.

17:28.714 --> 17:32.217
Maybe… …enjoy a glass
or two of wine with Candace.

17:32.301 --> 17:34.053
Watch a flick or something.

17:34.887 --> 17:37.222
I don't know, man, I was just…

17:37.306 --> 17:40.184
I decided to slide through the hood,
say what's up.

17:40.267 --> 17:42.686
-What the fuck you doing?
-Why the fuck you care?

17:42.770 --> 17:45.481
You kicked me out your house
on Thanksgiving, nigga.

17:45.564 --> 17:46.648
Yeah.

17:46.732 --> 17:51.320
In front of your family,
Jimmy, and Otis and Gail's uppity asses.

17:51.403 --> 17:54.198
-Nigga, all I was trying to do was--
-Yeah, I know. I… I know.

17:56.992 --> 17:59.578
I came here to apologize for how I acted.

18:00.496 --> 18:04.041
Uh… I've been going through some things
the last few years, and to be straight up,

18:04.124 --> 18:05.250
it's-- it's been rough.

18:06.251 --> 18:08.837
I think I finally got
this monkey off my back.

18:09.671 --> 18:11.173
I won, Dad.

18:12.216 --> 18:15.636
I got this motherfucker,
and if I can just finish this,

18:15.719 --> 18:17.721
then maybe I can spend
some more time with my family.

18:17.805 --> 18:20.474
Maybe I can be a better man
for Candace and Noah.

18:20.557 --> 18:23.852
Maybe I can find a way
for me and you, you know, for us to…

18:25.896 --> 18:27.189
get closer.

18:29.525 --> 18:32.986
-I don't know, I'm just saying shit.
-No, no, no, no, son.

18:34.696 --> 18:36.615
You saying what's on your heart.

18:39.701 --> 18:41.370
To be honest, I…

18:43.789 --> 18:44.665
Mm.

18:45.541 --> 18:47.960
I've been waiting
for this moment for a while.

18:50.254 --> 18:51.672
I prayed on it.

18:54.299 --> 18:57.553
It's not too late for us, Isaiah.

19:16.905 --> 19:19.616
I see you still got Josiah's chain on.

19:19.700 --> 19:21.785
-I miss him.
-Yeah.

19:21.869 --> 19:23.412
I miss him a lot.

19:23.495 --> 19:24.830
I miss him too.

19:25.747 --> 19:26.623
And your mama.

19:28.041 --> 19:31.086
Let's go inside and talk, man.
Let's get the fuck out of here, you know?

19:31.170 --> 19:34.214
-Just kick it. Crack some tall boys.
-I… You know, I… I got…

19:34.298 --> 19:37.467
-Trying to chill with my pops.
-Isaiah. Isaiah!

19:37.551 --> 19:40.179
You're the girl
Who makes me feel so good

19:40.262 --> 19:41.680
Cutie pie

19:45.017 --> 19:48.187
The kickback's closed, niggas. Get out.

19:49.188 --> 19:50.522
Get the fuck out right now!

19:51.315 --> 19:53.025
Noah, get the fuck over here.

19:57.196 --> 19:58.989
Smoking Zaza, huh?

19:59.948 --> 20:01.283
Trying to light up?

20:01.366 --> 20:03.493
Boy, I'm gonna light your ass up
all the way home.

20:03.577 --> 20:04.995
Get your narrow behind in that car.

20:05.078 --> 20:05.996
Get!

20:06.747 --> 20:08.582
My son, Amos.

20:08.665 --> 20:10.125
I knew you never changed, man!

20:10.209 --> 20:13.462
Slow down, boy. You coming in way too hot.

20:17.382 --> 20:19.927
-Shit!
-You don't deserve to wear this!

20:20.719 --> 20:22.012
You never did!

20:23.263 --> 20:25.140
I'm done with you, man.

20:25.224 --> 20:27.809
I'm done supporting you.
From now on, you're on your own.

20:29.353 --> 20:30.646
What you expect me to do?

20:30.729 --> 20:33.190
I expect you to go back to being
the base-level street nigga

20:33.273 --> 20:35.275
that you always was

20:35.359 --> 20:37.361
so I could do
what I should've done a long time ago,

20:37.444 --> 20:39.738
and lock your loser ass the fuck up!

20:40.489 --> 20:42.491
Noah, I said get in the car!

20:43.450 --> 20:45.077
What the fuck is you doing?

20:49.122 --> 20:50.499
Stiles offered me a deal.

20:50.582 --> 20:52.584
What are you gonna do?

20:58.715 --> 20:59.800
What am I gonna do?

21:00.884 --> 21:02.803
This nigga Stiles
could eat a fucking dick.

21:02.886 --> 21:05.138
-Fuck him and fuck the LAPD.
-Right.

21:05.222 --> 21:07.140
For all I know, he the cop who shot Deon.

21:07.224 --> 21:09.768
Matter of fact, he is the motherfucker
that killed my uncle,

21:09.851 --> 21:12.187
so fuck whatever
that bitch-ass nigga gotta say.

21:12.271 --> 21:14.523
-It's up for life!
-I need you two to hear this.

21:14.606 --> 21:17.067
You guys are my brothers,

21:17.150 --> 21:20.153
and I promise you both
we will make it out of this together.

21:20.862 --> 21:22.322
Deon did not die in vain.

21:22.406 --> 21:26.660
He died doing the most
honorable shit any of us could do.

21:26.743 --> 21:28.745
So now, we have to honor that.

21:29.329 --> 21:31.248
Somehow, we gonna make this right, man.

21:31.331 --> 21:33.083
Deon deserves that much.

21:33.166 --> 21:35.919
And Stiles deserves
much, much, much worse.

21:36.878 --> 21:40.048
He's the motherfucker
responsible for all of this.

21:40.799 --> 21:42.801
For all of it!

21:42.884 --> 21:44.678
He wants to take us out.

21:45.345 --> 21:47.889
He already took fucking Deon out.

21:47.973 --> 21:50.767
He took my money. He took my business.

21:50.851 --> 21:53.020
He took my fucking reputation.

21:54.563 --> 21:57.983
I swear on Deon's soul,

21:58.066 --> 22:01.028
we're gonna take
everything back from Stiles, everything!

22:03.697 --> 22:05.782
And we're gonna take it in blood.

22:15.459 --> 22:16.877
Hi, can I help you?

22:19.129 --> 22:24.843
I came to tell you Deon was killed
by the police three days ago.

22:29.681 --> 22:30.682
No.

22:31.308 --> 22:32.893
H-- How?

22:32.976 --> 22:35.103
I m-- How do you know?

22:36.938 --> 22:38.899
The police notified me.

22:39.775 --> 22:44.488
-Claimed his body yesterday.
-Notify? What?

22:44.571 --> 22:46.448
Who are you? What is your name?

22:46.531 --> 22:48.408
My name is Rena Davis.

22:49.618 --> 22:50.952
I'm Deon's wife.

22:55.332 --> 22:56.249
I didn't know.

22:58.502 --> 23:01.838
Yeah, well, I've known about you
for years, Melissa, so…

23:02.464 --> 23:03.965
Mommy!

23:04.049 --> 23:06.885
Hey. Hey, babies.

23:10.472 --> 23:13.308
You know, he always wanted twins.

23:14.017 --> 23:15.977
They look just like him.

23:16.061 --> 23:17.312
Come in?

23:17.396 --> 23:18.313
Yeah.

23:32.035 --> 23:34.579
We're working on
the arrest warrant for Wilder,

23:34.663 --> 23:36.248
but we need you to be patient, Stiles.

23:36.331 --> 23:38.542
Patient, man? Patient about what?

23:38.625 --> 23:41.420
I brought you a 16-point buck
on a silver platter.

23:41.503 --> 23:45.048
Now it's time to kill it and mount
that motherfucker on our mantle.

23:47.717 --> 23:49.553
Nice to see you, gentlemen.

23:50.220 --> 23:52.097
To what do we owe the honor, Breck?

23:52.180 --> 23:55.434
I'm here to inform you all
that I personally represent

23:55.517 --> 23:57.936
Ebony and Coltrane Wilder
in all legal matters.

23:58.019 --> 24:00.689
My firm has poured over
the basis for your warrants.

24:01.648 --> 24:03.066
And I have to say,

24:03.150 --> 24:06.194
guys, you really
screwed the pooch on this one.

24:06.278 --> 24:09.156
Your chain of both command and evidence

24:09.239 --> 24:13.994
are compromised by Lieutenant Stiles'
overzealous police work.

24:14.077 --> 24:16.872
All of your findings are circumstantial.

24:16.955 --> 24:20.292
At best, everything you have
is fruit from a poisonous tree.

24:20.959 --> 24:25.589
And at worst, the LAPD, city, and county
are looking at a nine-figure lawsuit

24:25.672 --> 24:28.425
that my firm and I cannot wait to file.

24:30.302 --> 24:32.429
Ebony and Coltrane Wilder are innocent,

24:32.512 --> 24:37.809
and any further actions will be met
with my firm's full force and might.

24:39.728 --> 24:41.313
You've been put on notice.

24:44.441 --> 24:45.901
Good day, gentlemen.

24:46.401 --> 24:48.195
Uh…

24:50.071 --> 24:51.865
What the fuck? All right.

24:51.948 --> 24:54.534
Fuck Randolph Duke
and his brother Mortimer.

24:54.618 --> 24:58.079
-Let's get this arrest warrant going.
-You know who that man is?

24:58.163 --> 25:00.081
His name is Breckinridge Peters.

25:00.165 --> 25:02.292
And we need to adjust our strategy.

25:02.375 --> 25:05.045
What? What strategy? We've won already.

25:05.128 --> 25:09.132
We've won nothing.
Nothing. I've never beaten Breck in court.

25:09.216 --> 25:10.592
What are you saying, Malik?

25:10.675 --> 25:12.260
He's saying you did a good job,

25:12.344 --> 25:14.638
but he can't give you
an arrest warrant yet.

25:15.847 --> 25:18.266
What? I got you the drugs.

25:18.350 --> 25:22.562
I got you the money.
I got you Deon Davis shooting cops.

25:22.646 --> 25:26.816
Yes, and we still aren't there yet.
Our searches have garnered us nil.

25:26.900 --> 25:29.903
The narcotics division is still up my ass
about the burnt-up warehouse,

25:29.986 --> 25:32.364
which has yet to produce anything of use.

25:32.447 --> 25:36.785
Meanwhile, the city has spent hundreds
of thousands of taxpayers' dollars

25:36.868 --> 25:39.788
and countless hours
of manpower on your case.

25:39.871 --> 25:41.998
As they should!

25:42.082 --> 25:44.793
Because we are dealing with murderers!

25:45.669 --> 25:47.462
What the fuck else do you want from me?

25:47.546 --> 25:52.884
We need you to calm down and start acting
like a rational adult for once.

25:52.968 --> 25:56.054
I can't give you an arrest warrant
with what we have.

25:56.137 --> 25:59.641
Especially with Breck and his firm
as their primary counsel.

26:01.476 --> 26:02.811
Hey, hold up, man.

26:03.562 --> 26:07.232
Wasn't you Mr. Man of the Year at that
Wilder-sponsored Black Illuminati gala?

26:07.315 --> 26:10.569
-You in on this shit with them too?
-That was your wife's idea.

26:10.652 --> 26:11.945
-What the…
-Enough, Isaiah!

26:12.028 --> 26:14.030
You in control of your report here, Jimmy?

26:14.114 --> 26:16.700
You think you know it all,
but you don't know shit, boy!

26:17.367 --> 26:19.494
I have a mind to take you
to that alley out back

26:19.578 --> 26:22.247
and squabble up
with your insubordinate ass.

26:22.330 --> 26:23.999
Get the fuck out of here.

26:24.082 --> 26:25.500
That's a goddamn order.

26:33.049 --> 26:34.426
Your boy's out of control.

28:08.853 --> 28:10.855
I know, but…

28:12.732 --> 28:14.776
Yeah, but come on, over some weed?

28:15.819 --> 28:19.698
He ain't have to cut you off like that,
Grandpa, he a real asshole for that.

28:20.490 --> 28:22.701
No, he do too much.

28:23.243 --> 28:26.121
And he snatched your chain off your neck.
What was that about?

28:26.204 --> 28:30.750
And how you gonna pay your bills now?
I'm… No, I'm just saying.

28:34.462 --> 28:36.423
-Nigga.
-Easy.

28:36.506 --> 28:38.717
Easy, I come in peace.

28:40.051 --> 28:44.347
Stiles, as much as I hate to admit it,
you actually did a great job back there.

28:44.431 --> 28:47.600
I mean, linking the wire
to the shell companies, to the warehouse,

28:47.684 --> 28:50.687
to Deon's suicide mission… Mwah!

28:50.770 --> 28:52.439
Chef's fucking kiss.

28:52.522 --> 28:56.192
You know, one might actually think
that you're good at this shit.

28:56.776 --> 29:00.196
The problem is, we need hard evidence.

29:02.365 --> 29:06.828
How far are you willing to go, Stiles?
You need to catch Wilder in the act.

29:06.911 --> 29:09.581
Smoking gun in hand.

29:09.664 --> 29:12.876
-By any means.
-So now you want me to do me.

29:12.959 --> 29:15.962
You slap cuffs on Coltrane Wilder legally,

29:16.045 --> 29:19.132
and I'll make sure everything
that you did to get there is fair play.

29:19.215 --> 29:20.592
For real?

29:24.637 --> 29:25.805
For real.

29:31.102 --> 29:32.520
Get the fuck away from me.

29:32.604 --> 29:36.232
-I'm here with a peace offering.
-What, Stiles?

29:36.316 --> 29:39.569
I got word from my snitch in Wayside
that Coltrane Wilder and his crew

29:39.652 --> 29:41.488
put out a hit on your CI.

29:41.571 --> 29:43.323
I do not know who your informant is,

29:43.406 --> 29:45.492
but a green light's
been authorized on him.

29:47.202 --> 29:49.454
I fucked up a few days ago, Marc.

29:50.121 --> 29:52.207
Trying to make up for it now.

29:52.290 --> 29:53.583
Before it's too late.

29:55.752 --> 29:57.462
How do I know it's even real?

29:57.545 --> 29:59.214
How do you know it's not?

30:00.048 --> 30:01.883
If I was you, I'd check up on him.

30:02.675 --> 30:04.219
In person.

30:38.253 --> 30:41.297
Thanks for meeting me here. Are you safe?

30:41.381 --> 30:43.591
Of course I'm safe. I'm always safe, bro.

30:43.675 --> 30:46.803
That's good, that's good,
because you still owe me.

30:47.428 --> 30:50.223
-I already did my job.
-That shitshow doesn't count.

30:50.306 --> 30:53.643
That fucker burned down the warehouse
along with all the fucking evidence.

30:53.726 --> 30:57.188
Look, I can't catch, clean,
cook, and serve the meal.

30:57.272 --> 31:00.942
-You have to do something.
-The program hasn't changed, aper.

31:01.025 --> 31:03.987
Until we catch the big fish,
you're still my bitch.

31:05.780 --> 31:07.282
Well, I got one for you.

31:07.365 --> 31:10.535
-Keep talking.
-The person who set up the whole deal.

31:10.618 --> 31:12.287
The middle man.

31:13.788 --> 31:14.622
I need a name.

31:14.706 --> 31:17.542
I'll tell you that
once I've done some damage control

31:17.625 --> 31:19.335
and I know things are back to normal.

31:19.419 --> 31:21.629
Well, you better make it snappy
and beef up security.

31:21.713 --> 31:25.091
Because according to my source,
that pill crew's coming for you.

31:26.342 --> 31:27.302
Okay.

31:27.886 --> 31:29.220
I'll add more men.

31:36.269 --> 31:38.396
What the fuck you doing here, homey?

31:41.566 --> 31:45.320
Your buddy Marc's CI is Andrei Malakian.

31:45.820 --> 31:47.906
Okay, what else you got for me?

31:47.989 --> 31:50.283
I looked up Andrei's rap sheet
in the system.

31:50.366 --> 31:54.287
He comes from a high-level
Armenian crime family, the Kurdjians.

31:54.370 --> 31:55.538
They're into everything.

31:55.622 --> 31:59.208
From narcotic distribution
to sex trafficking, extortion.

32:00.001 --> 32:02.211
Didn't their soldiers
kidnap that Alvarez girl?

32:06.174 --> 32:08.927
If I were Coltrane Wilder,
what would I want right now?

32:09.010 --> 32:10.428
To leave town.

32:12.055 --> 32:14.307
No, I'd want revenge.

32:15.558 --> 32:17.477
We need to find out
where Andrei's holed up

32:17.560 --> 32:19.938
and lay on him
until Wilder's crew comes for him.

32:20.021 --> 32:23.066
-I can follow Marc again.
-No, no, no, that won't work.

32:24.943 --> 32:28.529
I know a really bad guy
who owes me a really big favor.

32:28.613 --> 32:30.740
-I'll get my coat.
-You gotta stay here.

32:30.823 --> 32:34.702
Brinkley, if anything goes wrong,
it'll be just me on the line for this.

32:35.787 --> 32:38.414
You did great work. Proud of you.

32:38.498 --> 32:40.291
No, for real, I'm proud of you.

32:42.085 --> 32:43.336
Now get out of here.

32:47.340 --> 32:48.549
Yes, of course.

32:48.633 --> 32:52.136
Of course I'll help you select the next
Baldwin Hills Cares Man of the Year.

32:52.220 --> 32:54.764
-That'd be an honor.
-Oh, thank you so much.

32:55.556 --> 32:56.432
Of course.

32:56.516 --> 32:59.227
I am so excited that you are excited.

32:59.310 --> 33:00.269
Mm-hmm.

33:00.353 --> 33:02.981
Honestly,
I was a little nervous for a second.

33:03.064 --> 33:07.151
-Why would you be nervous?
-Oh, I have so much going on in life.

33:07.235 --> 33:09.487
You know, at home with…

33:12.073 --> 33:13.950
I did see Isaiah today.

33:14.575 --> 33:16.494
-Oh.
-Is he all right?

33:16.577 --> 33:17.954
Huh…

33:18.037 --> 33:20.039
Are you all right?

33:20.748 --> 33:23.209
Come on, it's okay.
You know you could tell me.

33:23.292 --> 33:25.461
I'm a safe space for you.
I always have been.

33:27.338 --> 33:33.052
It's just… Isaiah hasn't been himself
for, like, the past two years.

33:33.553 --> 33:35.972
More so, like the past few months.

33:36.931 --> 33:40.351
This case he's working, it's just--
It's pushing him over the edge.

33:40.435 --> 33:44.731
I don't know how much more I can handle
for my sake or the sake of my son.

33:44.814 --> 33:45.982
Okay, how about this?

33:46.774 --> 33:50.611
I can't help you with Isaiah,
but I can help with Noah.

33:52.613 --> 33:53.865
Why don't you let me mentor him

33:53.948 --> 33:56.242
through the Baldwin Hills
Cares Stewardship Program?

33:57.368 --> 34:00.038
That way, he can have
a positive Black male role model

34:00.121 --> 34:01.914
who's consistent in his life.

34:02.498 --> 34:05.084
Oh yeah,
that would be wonderful, actually.

34:05.960 --> 34:09.005
Noah really could use
some balance in his life right now.

34:09.088 --> 34:12.341
-Of course.
-And honestly, so could I.

34:41.746 --> 34:43.164
Andrei Malakian.

34:43.748 --> 34:46.542
I need to know
where he's holed up at right now.

34:46.626 --> 34:47.919
It's a matter of life or death.

34:49.462 --> 34:52.965
I love a high-stakes situation.

34:53.925 --> 34:55.927
Cuéntame. Tell me more.

34:59.305 --> 35:01.265
You're at war with the Armenians.

35:02.391 --> 35:04.894
What I am asking you for

35:04.977 --> 35:09.023
may be of mutual benefit
to both your organization and mine.

35:09.107 --> 35:12.985
You are aware, if I do this, we're even.

35:13.069 --> 35:13.903
I know.

35:15.404 --> 35:18.616
-Business is business.
-Negocios son negocios.

35:28.501 --> 35:32.380
Give me until tomorrow.
You'll have your information.

35:38.719 --> 35:40.596
Whoever's responsible for this shit,

35:41.180 --> 35:43.516
we're gonna put them in a backwood
and smoke 'em.

35:43.599 --> 35:45.560
I know who's responsible.

35:45.643 --> 35:47.145
That foo' Andrei.

35:47.228 --> 35:49.397
-The Armenian?
-Mm-hmm.

35:49.480 --> 35:52.233
I followed him from his crib in Glendale
like you told me to.

35:52.316 --> 35:53.901
That piece of shit ain't just hot.

35:53.985 --> 35:57.363
He's an informant for narcotics,
maybe even robbery homicide.

35:57.446 --> 36:00.491
This whole shit
was one big setup from jump.

36:00.575 --> 36:03.327
He's giving them your guy,
the one who gives us the jobs.

36:03.411 --> 36:05.788
Andrei lined us up
to steal that load and get popped.

36:05.872 --> 36:07.874
He's the real reason Deon got killed.

36:09.167 --> 36:12.378
Who do we focus on, 'Trane?
Andrei or Stiles?

36:14.297 --> 36:17.967
Both of them. We're gonna up the score
on each one of these motherfuckers.

36:18.050 --> 36:22.847
I have a way for us to fuck over Stiles
and Andrei same time and get away clean.

36:22.930 --> 36:25.016
Because these two don't get to win. We do.

36:25.099 --> 36:28.352
-What's the plan, bro?
-We're gonna hit Andrei. Hard.

36:28.436 --> 36:31.731
Three-man team, going strong
through the front, direct and deadly.

36:31.814 --> 36:33.399
Shit, nigga, you know I'm with it.

36:33.482 --> 36:35.860
What if the cops come?
They're probably watching him, right?

36:35.943 --> 36:38.321
Then we hit them too,
with overwhelming force.

36:38.404 --> 36:39.697
Cops, they not ready for that.

36:39.780 --> 36:44.118
The only issue is, each minute we're still
on the scene, more cops will come,

36:44.202 --> 36:46.078
and they become the overwhelming force.

36:46.162 --> 36:50.625
So if we do bang it out,
we do it strong and succinct.

36:51.834 --> 36:52.960
Hey, man, look.

36:53.669 --> 36:57.340
You know I'm ready to ride
for my uncle and for us.

36:57.423 --> 36:59.926
But I gotta make it home to my family too.

37:00.760 --> 37:03.596
Now, we gonna do
what we motherfucking gotta do.

37:03.679 --> 37:07.934
Whatever it takes, whatever we face,
I don't give a fuck, nigga. It's wartime.

37:08.017 --> 37:12.063
I'll kill Andrei, Stiles, and the whole
motherfucking LAPD if I got to.

37:12.730 --> 37:14.774
But I'm making it home to my babies, bro.

37:14.857 --> 37:17.026
We all making it home, brother.

37:21.030 --> 37:22.490
Andrei back in Glendale?

37:22.573 --> 37:26.744
Nah, he didn't return to the house.
And all of his bodyguards are gone too.

37:27.328 --> 37:29.622
Might've been spooked by his handler.
He knows we're coming.

37:29.705 --> 37:33.751
I'm glad he knows we're coming.
Let him live his last days in fear.

37:35.503 --> 37:38.547
I'll find out where he is.
Just be on go when I send the word.

37:55.398 --> 37:56.565
A toast.

37:57.525 --> 37:58.818
To Deon.

37:58.901 --> 38:00.695
He was my best friend.

38:02.071 --> 38:03.406
He was my heart.

38:04.031 --> 38:06.284
A gentleman among gentlemen.

38:06.367 --> 38:08.077
King amongst kings.

38:08.661 --> 38:10.496
Killer amongst killers.

38:10.579 --> 38:13.291
We love you, and we miss you.

38:14.667 --> 38:15.751
Salud.

38:22.258 --> 38:23.968
-Love you guys.
-I love you, bro.

38:24.051 --> 38:25.136
Yeah, man.

38:28.180 --> 38:29.181
Love you.

38:31.517 --> 38:33.269
-I love you, fam.
-I love you, man.

38:44.947 --> 38:47.033
He's been on a lone wolf mission.

38:47.116 --> 38:49.618
All he cares about is his case, and…

38:50.953 --> 38:53.080
And I can't keep up anymore.

